On Sat, Apr 09, 2005 at 05:50:18PM +0200, alpha-linux at gmx.net wrote:
> 
> on i386 you can specify "linux askmethod" during boot.
> is this available as well an alpha and how ?

If you are booting via aboot from SRM then

   b dqa200 -fl i

(substitute "dqa200" with whatever is a name used by SRM for your boot
device) and you will get an aboot prompt where you can list and choose
from all predefined boot commands.  If none is suitable you can type a
full boot command yourself. "i" is short for "interactive".

If you already set 'bootdef_dev' to your boot device name then 'b -fl i'
will be enough.

   Michal



